c": null}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "In Search of an Understandable Consensus Algorithm – the morning...", "content": "Raft implements consensus by first electing a distinguished leader, then giving the leader complete responsibility for managing the replicated log.Raft divides time into terms, each beginning with an election. If a candidate wins the election, they stay as leader for the rest of the term.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [6], "score": 0.16666666666666666, "category": "general", "url": "https://blog.acolyer.org/2015/03/12/in-search-of-an-understandable-consensus-algorithm/", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "blog.acolyer.org", "/2015/03/12/in-search-of-an-understandable-consensus-algorithm/", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "Dynatune: Dynamic Tuning of Raft Election Parameters Using...", "content": "The OTS time is directly influenced by election parameters, such as heartbeat interval and election timeout.Here, broadcastTime is the average time required for a server to send RPCs in parallel to all other servers in the cluster and receive their responses.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [7], "score": 0.14285714285714285, "category": "general", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.15154", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "arxiv.org", "/pdf/2507.15154", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "AI-Driven Consensus -- Part 1", "content": "Raft Consensus in Container Orchestration: Docker Swarm, Kubernetes etcd, and AI-Augmented Cluster Management. Raft is a leader-based consensus algorithm for building replicated state machines.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [8], "score": 0.125, "category": "general", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-driven-consensus-part-1-sepehr-sedigh-mhylf", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "www.linkedin.com", "/pulse/ai-driven-consensus-part-1-sepehr-sedigh-mhylf", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "Raft consensus algorithm", "content": "Raft uses randomized election timeouts to elect leaders.Consensus Algorithm: An algorithm used to achieve agreement on a single data value among distributed processes or systems. Raft and Paxos are examples of consensus algorithms.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [9], "score": 0.1111111111111111, "category": "general", "url": "https://www.chriswirz.com/distributed-systems/raft", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "www.chriswirz.com", "/distributed-systems/raft", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "Raft Consensus Algorithm - Speaker Deck", "content": "Raft timing and availability Raft timing and availability Timing is. critical in Raft to elect and maintain a steady leader over time, in order to have a perfect availability of the cluster.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [10], "score": 0.1, "category": "general", "url": "https://speakerdeck.com/isopropylcyanide/raft-consensus-algorithm", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "speakerdeck.com", "/isopropylcyanide/raft-consensus-algorithm", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "Raft Consensus Algorithm | Explainers", "content": "Each follower maintains an election timeout — a random interval between 150-300ms. If a follower doesn't hear from a leader before this timeout expires, it takes action.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [11], "score": 0.09090909090909091, "category": "general", "url": "https://www.ketankhairnar.com/explainers/raft-consensus/", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "www.ketankhairnar.com", "/explainers/raft-consensus/", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "'Introduction to the Raft algorithm' · 蚂蚁云原生架构SOFAStack", "content": "Introduction to Raft algorithms. Distributed consensus - Raft and JRaft. Other. How to contribute to SOFAJRaft. 'Introduction to the Raft algorithm'.Summary of the Raft consensus algorithm. Election safety. At most one leader can be elected in a given term.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [12], "score": 0.08333333333333333, "category": "general", "url": "https://www.sofastack.tech/en/projects/sofa-jraft/raft-introduction/", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "www.sofastack.tech", "/en/projects/sofa-jraft/raft-introduction/", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "Notes on Raft, the consensus protocol | Cracking The Code", "content": "Raft consensus algorithm. It elects a leader as the first thing before everything else.electionTimeout: Time for which a server waits for a leader to be elected. If no leader is elected within this time, the server starts a new term and a new election is initiated.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [13], "score": 0.07692307692307693, "category": "general", "url": "https://igupta.in/blog/notes-on-raft/", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "igupta.in", "/blog/notes-on-raft/", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "In Search of An Understandable Consensus Algorithm: A Summary", "content": "Raft divides time into terms of arbitrary length, each beginning with an election. If a candidate wins the election, it stays leader for the rest of the term. If the vote is split, then that term ends without a leader.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [14], "score": 0.07142857142857142, "category": "general", "url": "https://practicaldev-herokuapp-com.global.ssl.fastly.net/shubheksha/in-search-of-an-understandable-consensus-algorithm-a-summary-b83", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["https", "practicaldev-herokuapp-com.global.ssl.fastly.net", "/shubheksha/in-search-of-an-understandable-consensus-algorithm-a-summary-b83", "", "", ""]}, {"template": "default.html", "title": "In Search of an Understandable Consensus Algorithm", "content": "• Leader election: Raft uses randomized timers to elect leaders. This adds only a small amount of mechanism to the heartbeats already required for any consensus algorithm, while resolving conicts sim-ply and rapidly.", "img_src": "", "iframe_src": "", "audio_src": "", "thumbnail": "", "publishedDate": null, "pubdate": "", "length": null, "views": "", "author": "", "metadata": "", "priority": "", "engines": ["yandex"], "open_group": false, "close_group": false, "positions": [15], "score": 0.06666666666666667, "category": "general", "url": "http://man6.org/blog/papers/In_Search_of_an_Understandable_Consensus_Algorithm.pdf", "engine": "yandex", "parsed_url": ["http", "man6.org", "/blog/papers/In_Search_of_an_Understandable_Consensus_Algorithm.pdf", "", "", ""]}], "answers": [], "corrections": [], "infoboxes": [], "suggestions": [], "unresponsive_engines": []}}
